supernatural sam and dean winchester  played by jared padalecki and jensen  ackles battled legions of monsters for  15 seasons alongside countless guest  stars  some left until their characters  returned to life some left because their  characters were misunderstood  and some left for other reasons find out  why they really said goodbye  mark shepherd played crowley the demonic  king of hell  in seasons 5 through 12 and he became an  integral part of the show  he secretly aided and openly antagonized  the winchester brothers acting as a  friend or foe whenever it was most  convenient for his purposes  but shepard felt that his character  deserved a better send off from the show  than the way his final exit was written  in which he sacrificed himself on an  angel's blade  in a fan q a he expressed his  disappointment saying  once they decided they needed to do  something different with the direction  of the show  they tried to get rid of me without  telling me that they were going to get  rid of me  i'd gone from being the smartest  character on the show to being the  dumbest character on the show in two  seasons they ran out of what to do  no one in the history of torch has been  tortured with torture  like the torture you'll be tortured with  needless to say  shepard did not part company with the  show on the best of terms dj quarles  joined supernatural in season seven as  demon hunter garfitzgerald  who preferred working alone but was  occasionally willing to team up with the  winchesters  he later underwent an intense  transformation when he became a  werewolf quarles was very appreciative  of the fan's enthusiastic support  and said he had loved working on  supernatural but there was simply no  room in his schedule to return to the  show  he told tv guide i'm so busy right now  i'm on a couple different shows and i  have two films lined up after this  he regretted having let the supernatural  fandom down and promised to make time  for the show  eventually returning for guest spots in  seasons 14 and 15.  katie cassidy was the first actress on  the show to play ruby  a demon who almost tore the winchester  brothers close relationship apart  cassidy said she felt that leaving  supernatural was heartbreaking  why did she exit despite loving her time  on the show so much  according to series creator eric kripke  the production company could no longer  afford to keep her on the payroll but  cassidy offered a slightly different  explanation  she told tv guide warner brothers wasn't  exactly sure what they were going to do  with my character  and i had the option to stay or leave  when harper's island came about i was  really into it so i asked them to let me  go  luckily they did when genevieve cortezi  joined the cast of supernatural in  season 4 to take over the role of the  demon ruby  she didn't expect that it would  completely change her life  but ruby's scandalous on-screen  relationship with sam winchester  blossomed into genevieve's real-life  romance with jared patalecki who  admitted that he waited about  four months before asking her on a date  his patience paid off in a big way  they were married not long after the  fourth season wreck  and she became genevieve padalecki  in 2012 genevieve gave birth to the  couple's first child  a son named thomas and then their  children austin and odette arrived soon  after in 2013 and 2017.  hadalecki has focused on family since  then largely retiring from acting but  did return  to supernatural for a guest spot in the  final season  jeffrey dean morgan was an original cast  member on supernatural  he played sam and dean's father john  winchester who became a demon hunter  after his wife sam and dean's mother was  killed by a demon  given how important he was in the  brothers lives having sent them down  their path  it's surprising he doesn't appear much  past season 3.  although the showrunners had wanted to  keep him on and feature him more after  season 2  morgan's busy schedule left them with no  choice writer's sarah gamble told  digital spy  we would love to have him back but he's  really busy he's turned into a huge star  over here  we got to use his voice for an episode  at the end of last season so there's  always a chance we would love to bring  back the character  if our schedules ever lined up but i  don't think anyone should hold their  breath  thankfully morgan was able to return for  several guest spots as jon in later  seasons of the show  alona tall became part of the  supernatural cast in season 2  as joe harvell whose mother ellen was a  friend of the winchester's dad  joe teamed up with him to hunt demons  until her death and appeared as a ghost  in season 7  then never returned again tall said that  she would have embraced the opportunity  to appear on supernatural again as joe  but she worried that the show's new  leadership didn't seem to fully  understand what she  and samantha ferris who had played her  mother had brought to the table  she told mea worldwide i think what  happened  was that when samantha and i were part  of the show there were different heads  of creative  but the people running things there have  changed and i don't think they know us  very well  or know our characters she also stated  that she hoped to appear in the series  final season  but it didn't pan out julian richings  played death himself  also known as the grim reaper or the  pale horseman on supernatural  his appearances were rare but  unforgettable especially considering  death's weakness for fattening food  he just couldn't resist eating a meal at  a diner richings made his final  appearance as death in season 10 and in  the following seasons  lisa berry took over the role by the  time his last episode had come around  richings had already taken on a new  recurring role  as the shadowy benjamin kirtland on  orphan black  and it was the perfect time to step away  richings always seemed to have a full  schedule  and since then he's landed roles on  series including 12 monkeys and doom  patrol  richard spade jr played the archangel  gabriel disguised as the trickster loki  though always mischievous gabriel  eventually sided with the winchesters  gabriel met his end in season 13 but as  it turned out  spate himself never really left  supernatural at all  in addition to acting spate left his  mark by directing several episodes of  the series including some in the final  season  he was behind the camera for proverbs 17  3  our father who aren't in heaven and  galaxy brain  kurt fuller appeared on supernatural as  the villainous angel  zechariah fuller embraced the chance to  play an unsaintly bad guy and ended up  really enjoying it in fact he felt a  little guilty about it  admitting to himself he needed a change  fuller jumped at the opportunity to join  the situation comedy better with you  which he described as a welcome relief  after his time on supernatural  he told staying in making people laugh  rather than making people bleed is much  more fun  and i feel better about it this is  definitely better for my soul  carrie anne fleming appeared on  supernatural as karen singer  wife of supporting character bobby  singer she had been possessed by a demon  and then killed by her husband bobby who  didn't understand the paranormal nature  of what had happened to her  fleming's first guest appearance on the  show was marred by personal troubles  as she struggled with postpartum  depression at the time  sadly she was also preparing to leave  her marriage  fleming would later joke to fans that  white clown makeup and no sleep was all  it took to make her look like a genuine  zombie but at the time  she was so deeply troubled she could  barely get through a day on set  she told times colonists i was having  trouble being happy  i had trouble memorizing dialogue and  communicating  she did return to supernatural in season  seven which was hopefully a better  experience  fans of supernatural know rick worthy as  the alpha vampire the very first member  of the vampire species but when worthy  first auditioned  he had wanted to play a much more  prominent and longer-term role  crowley he told digital spy i really  wanted to be on the show and i had  auditioned probably  five or six times before i auditioned  for the role of crowley which i thought  was a great role  and was devastated just devastated when  i didn't get it  unfortunately because worthy wasn't  chosen for a major role he couldn't stay  on supernatural as long as he'd really  wanted  he went on to other roles including the  strict dean fogg on the magicians  when we freaks die  where do we go not heaven  not hell so  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

